testing yupiter
===============

Build and run:

    ./configure --enable-tests=yes
    make
    make check

The runner is test/run-tests.sh.  It prints one PASS or FAIL per check
and exits non-zero on any failure.


Registered checks
-----------------

Golden output, merged golden output, reference comparison, self-checking,
fatal paths, write destinations, mocked syscall, installation, archive
inspection.  The last check stages an install into build/install-test
and builds a consumer with pkg-config and CMake.


Golden files
------------

Regenerate from the host C library, never from yupiter:

    cc -std=c17 -DYUPITER_REFERENCE -w test/format.c -o /tmp/reference-format
    /tmp/reference-format > /tmp/expected-format.txt
    diff -u test/expected-format.txt /tmp/expected-format.txt

See the golden-files job in .github/workflows/build-test.yml.


Adding a test
-------------

Add the program in test/, its name in mk/variables.mk, and its check in
test/run-tests.sh.  The pattern rule in mk/tests.mk covers ordinary
freestanding tests.